#kaocha/v1
{:tests
 [{:id :unit
   ;; The ^:integration tests drive a REAL tmux server through libtmux, so they
   ;; need a session and the conda hive env. Without those they take the
   ;; (when (ensure-python!) ...) branch and assert nothing, which kaocha
   ;; correctly reports as a FAILURE rather than a pass: a test that ran no
   ;; assertions proved nothing.
   ;;
   ;; Skipping by metadata is the honest form. kaocha reports them as skipped,
   ;; so the count says what was not run instead of hiding it inside a green
   ;; total. Run them deliberately:
   ;;   clojure -M:test --focus-meta :integration
   :kaocha.filter/skip-meta [:integration]}]}
